{"type":"standard","title":"Jaqaru language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jaqaru language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q33443","titles":{"canonical":"Jaqaru_language","normalized":"Jaqaru language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jaqaru language</span></span>"},"pageid":1918627,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Jaqaru.png/330px-Jaqaru.png","width":330,"height":261},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8e/Jaqaru.png","width":580,"height":458},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1345741394","tid":"682d7afe-2a2a-11f1-a864-ec907f734a64","timestamp":"2026-03-27T22:15:05Z","description":"Aymaran language spoken in Peru","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaqaru_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaqaru_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaqaru_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jaqaru_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaqaru_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Jaqaru_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaqaru_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jaqaru_language"}},"extract":"Jaqaru or Jacaru is a language of the Aymaran family. It is also known as Jaqi and Aru. It is spoken in the districts of Tupe and Catahuasi in Yauyos Province, Lima Region, Peru. Most of the 2,000 ethnic Jaqaru have migrated to Lima.","extract_html":"<p><b>Jaqaru</b> or <b>Jacaru</b> is a language of the Aymaran family. It is also known as <b>Jaqi</b> and <b>Aru</b>. It is spoken in the districts of Tupe and Catahuasi in Yauyos Province, Lima Region, Peru. Most of the 2,000 ethnic Jaqaru have migrated to Lima.</p>"}